WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.496
The paper makes two contributions.

00:00:03.576 --> 00:00:07.073
First,

00:00:07.153 --> 00:00:10.649
a differentiable regularization for graphs: a
learnable permutation that lines nodes into

00:00:10.729 --> 00:00:14.225
a single row while preserving permutation invariance,

00:00:14.305 --> 00:00:17.801
so Euclidean convolution finally applies.

00:00:17.881 --> 00:00:21.378
Second, the model built on it, the Compressed
Convolution Network, or CoCN.

00:00:21.458 --> 00:00:24.954
It learns both node and structure features and
trains end to end,

00:00:25.034 --> 00:00:28.530
beating competitive GNNs and pooling models.
